<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex details Q2 hydrocarbon trade.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex details Q2 hydrocarbon trade.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) reported its exports and imports of crude oil, petroleum products, natural gas and chemicals for the second quarter. Figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>    Item		  Q2 1997	Pct change from Q2 '96</p>
<p>    Balance		 2,209		 -13.8</p>
<p>	Exports	     2,662		  -7.6</p>
<p>	Imports		 453		  42.2</p>
<p>    Crude Exports	 2,489		  -5.0</p>
<p>    Petroleum Products   -393		 108.4</p>
<p>	Exports		  38		 -66.3</p>
<p>	Imports		 431		  42.6</p>
<p>    Natural Gas		-7		   n/a</p>
<p>   Exports		     10		 -25.8</p>
<p>	Imports		  16		  31.0</p>
<p>    Petrochemicals	  120		  -9.3</p>
<p>	Exports		 125		  -7.7</p>
<p>	Imports		   6		  46.0</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903. E-mail at timna.tanners@reuter.com))</p>
</text>
